//RS /// or `None` if the handle is only ever used in place (as the receiver of a
//RS /// method call / field access / `?` on itself). The receiver of `handle.read(…)`
//RS /// is an in-place use (performing the authorized effect); everything else — `return
//RS /// handle`, `x :: handle`, `f(handle)`, `[handle]`, a struct field, an `or`
